# Ripple ActivityWatch listener — Windows env
# This file ships with the credentials baked in for the 5/22 demo. Treat as
# semi-secret: anyone with this key can write to the Supabase device_activity
# table (no other tables — RLS / role scope still applies on the project).
#
# After demo, rotate VITE_SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY and re-distribute.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ubuamehrsvyrbnoxtavk.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=<paste key from chat — see README>

# Optional — override the auto-derived device name shown on the Ripple dashboard.
# Default on Windows is "Windows PC · <hostname>". Uncomment + edit if you want
# something punchier like "YorHa Desktop" or "Gaming Rig · Win11".
# AW_DISPLAY_NAME=YorHa Desktop

# Optional — override the stable device_id used as the Supabase upsert key.
# Default on Windows is `win-<hostname>`. Don't change unless you have a reason
# (changing this makes the dashboard treat it as a NEW device).
# AW_DEVICE_ID=win-yorha-desktop

# Optional — override Supabase user_id this device reports under.
# Default is `tommychen030607` (matches the demo account).
# RIPPLE_USER_ID=tommychen030607

# Optional — change polling interval (ms). Default 30 000 = every 30 s.
# AW_POLL_MS=30000

# Optional — change AW host (default http://localhost:5600).
# AW_HOST=http://localhost:5600
